== Conditions to Make Angel Rooms Appear ==
For the player to have a chance to get an Angel Room after killing a boss (or with a {{p|Joker}} card / {{e|Red Chest}} teleport), some conditions must be met:
* A {{R|Devil Room}} door has spawned on any previous floor.
** Teleporting to a {{R|Devil Room}} with a {{p|Joker}} card or a {{e|Red Chest}} doesn't count.
** {{dlc+|r}} {{i|Book of Virtues}} and the "You feel blessed!" fortune from {{M|Confessional}}s make the first deal to appear in a run to be an Angel Room.{{dlc-}}
* No [[Devil Room#Deals with the Devil|Deals with the Devil]] have been made throughout the run.
** Taking {{e|Red Chest}} items, using {{p|Credit Card}}, using {{i|Coupon}}, or collecting an item from {{E|Krampus}} do not count.
** Even though it technically doesn't cost any health, taking a devil deal with {{c|The Lost}} will still prevent Angel Rooms from appearing.
** {{dlc+|r}} Paying for {{R|Devil Room}} items from Boss Rooms after using {{i|Satanic Bible}} will still prevent Angel Rooms from spawning.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} {{i|Book of Virtues}} and {{i|Act of Contrition}} allow for Angel Rooms to spawn even if a Devil Deal was taken previously, as well as allowing to take Devil Deals without being locked out of Angel Rooms.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} The "You feel blessed!" fortune from {{M|Confessional}}s allow for Angel Rooms to spawn even if a Devil Deal was taken previously, but only for the current floor.{{dlc-}}

=== {{dlc|a}} Sacrifice Room Exception ===
* On the 3rd and 5th sacrifice in a {{R|Sacrifice Room}}, there is a 66% chance that the player will receive the "You feel blessed!" effect. This will increase the chances of the Angel Room spawning even if the previous conditions have not been met.
* On the 6th sacrifice in a {{R|Sacrifice Room}}, there is a 33% chance that the player will be teleported to the Angel Room if they haven't already visited or opened the Devil Room for that floor. This will occur even if the previous conditions have not been met.

== Angel Room Generation Chance ==
The selection between Angel Room and Devil Room is made upon opening the door after defeating the floor's boss (or upon teleporting to the room using a {{p|Joker}} card or a {{e|Red Chest}}).

The game makes a series of coin flips to determine if an Angel Room will appear or not. If one of these coin flips succeeds, an Angel Room is generated (except for the Devil beggar coin flip). If all the coin flips fail or no coin flips are done, a Devil Room is generated. Satisfying certain conditions gives additional coin flips with varying probabilities:

